  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A source emitting a sound of frequency <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"f_{0}\"></span> is approaching an observer. At time <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t=0\"></span> the source begins to decelerate and comes to rest when <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t=T\"></span>. The source does not pass the observer.</p>\n<p>The speed of the source is always much less than the speed of sound.</p>\n<p>What is the variation with t of the relative change of frequency <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\Delta  f}{{f}_{0}}\"></span> of the observed sound?</p>\n<p><br/></p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>[1]</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">Option A is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"B\">Option B is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"C\">Option C is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"D\">Option D is shown in the figure above.</li></ol>"
